SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20250608T070000Z
DTSTART:20250608T070000Z
DTEND:20250608T082500Z
SUMMARY:Customer Portal Maintenance
DESCRIPTION:We will be undergoing scheduled maintenance to the database of
  the Customers Portal (https://customers.gitlab.com) from 05:00 UTC to 06:
 25 UTC on 8th of June 2025. GitLab.com will continue to be available durin
 g the maintenance window. The Customers Portal will be temporarily unavail
 able at some point during this maintenance window\, which will mean custom
 ers who have purchased licenses and intend to activate them may need to wa
 it until the end of the maintenance window to activate their licenses. We 
 apologize in advance for any inconvenience this may cause. For further det
 ails see - https://gitlab.com/gitlab-com/gl-infra/production/-/issues/1962
 4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0000x0ft6i@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20250419T060000Z
DTSTART:20250419T060000Z
DTEND:20250419T120000Z
SUMMARY:Decomposition of security database in GitLab.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a scheduled maintenance event to conduct the decomposi
 tion of tables relating to Gitlab's Security Risk Management features to a
  new DB cluster in GitLab.com's infrastructure to improve scalability and 
 reliability.\n\nWe expect very little disruption during this process. Ther
 e may be increased latency and/or requests errors for a small duration\, b
 ut we do not expect any downtime during transition.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0000ubctr9@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20250401T133000Z
DTSTART:20250401T133000Z
DTEND:20250411T133000Z
SUMMARY:Change in OAuth grant support
DESCRIPTION:GitLab.com is improving the security of OAuth Resource Owner P
 assword Credentials grant type and will require client authentication for 
 all ROPC requests\, effective April 8\, 2025.\n\nMore information about th
 is change can be read here: https://about.gitlab.com/blog/2025/04/01/impro
 ving-oauth-ropc-security-on-gitlab-com/
END:VEVENT
