UID:000-jn624z@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20211113T020000Z
DTSTART:20211113T020000Z
DTEND:20211113T050000Z
SUMMARY:Scheduled Maintenance on customers.gitlab.com
DESCRIPTION:customers.gitlab.com will be unavailable during the maintenanc
 e window due to a 3rd-party API set to maintenance mode. Customers won't b
 e able to manage their subscriptions or purchase new ones.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0000dvplpr@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20210710T090000Z
DTSTART:20210710T090000Z
DTEND:20210710T090500Z
SUMMARY:GitLab.com datastore maintainence activity - 10 July 2021
DESCRIPTION:As part of a maintenance activity on the GitLab.com datastore\
 , we will be conducting a switchover from the current primary database nod
 e to a read replica node. \n\nUsers should be expecting 50X errors for a v
 ery brief span of time during this window. See gitlab.com/gitlab-com/gl-in
 fra/production/-/issues/4781. 
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0000tyh2fm@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20210508T090000Z
DTSTART:20210508T090000Z
DTEND:20210508T100000Z
SUMMARY:GitLab.com PostgreSQL Database Upgrade
DESCRIPTION:We'll be upgrading GitLab.com PostgreSQL database to version 1
 2. This maintenance will include primary transition of the cluster within 
 a 1 hour window with downtime during part or all of the window.\n\nWe inte
 nd to minimize the length of downtime\, but you should plan for all servic
 es will be unavailable during the hour maintenance. \n\nWhy are we doing t
 his upgrade?\n1. Keeping up with new Gitlab.com release support\n2. Genera
 l improvements available in newer versions of PostgreSQL\n3. Specific impr
 ovements in the PostgreSQL query planner which have recently led to perfor
 mance impacts and service disruptions for GitLab.com\n\nWhy does it requir
 e downtime?\nThe upgrade approach requires a short downtime while we trans
 ition all services from the existing PostgreSQL cluster to this new versio
 n 12 PostgreSQL cluster and ensure that all runtime and asynchronous funct
 ions are operating as expected.\n\nAdditional information is available in 
 this GitLab Issue: https://gitlab.com/gitlab-com/gl-infra/production/-/iss
 ues/4037
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:000-qip0tw@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20210507T144500Z
DTSTART:20210507T144500Z
DTEND:20210507T145000Z
SUMMARY:Unscheduled maintenance - Switchover of our primary database
DESCRIPTION:We will be conducting a switchover of our primary database at 
 14:45 UTC to mitigate a potential instability. Users will be unable to acc
 ess GitLab.com for up to 2 minutes during this switchover. Please check ht
 tps://gitlab.com/gitlab-com/gl-infra/production/-/issues/4528
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:000-z8lv59@status.io
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20210401T020000Z
DTSTART:20210401T020000Z
DTEND:20210401T030000Z
SUMMARY:GitLab.com available from additional IPs beginning 2021-04-01
DESCRIPTION:Beginning 2021-04-01\, GitLab.com will add a second IP range f
 or traffic from it's Web and API fleet (34.74.226.0/24). \n\nGitLab.com us
 ers with specific access controls for inbound traffic (such as webhooks or
  repository mirroring) may need to update their allowlists.\n\nWhile this 
 change is scheduled for April 1st\, customers are encouraged to make this 
 update as soon as possible. It may become necessary for us to implement th
 is change earlier than the scheduled date in response to an incident invol
 ving this functionality.\n\nDetails can be found in: docs.gitlab.com/ee/us
 er/gitlab_com/#ip-range
END:VEVENT
